date their client to support fetching the\ncorresponding full CRL when it has been regenerated; otherwise, some serial\nnumbers may not appear in the local copy of the full CRL if the remote\ncomplete and delta CRLs has been regenerated.`),mdx(\"p\",null,`Endpoints with source `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`local`),` only include cluster-local revocations. When\nthe `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`unified_crl`),` parameters is enabled in the `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"#set-crl-configuration\"},`CRL\nconfiguration`),`, endpoints with source `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`unified`),`\nwill have revocations from all clusters. Generally use of the `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`unified`),`\nsource is more consistent with expectations of external apps, but see\nthe `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/docs/secrets/pki/considerations\"},`PKI Considerations`),` page\nfor a discussion on cluster size and unified CRLs/OCSP.`),mdx(\"p\",null,`CRL entries for certificates revoked with a non-zero `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`revocation_reason`),` include\nthe RFC 5280 Reason Code extension (OID 2.5.29.21).`),mdx(EnterpriseAlert,{product:\"vault\",mdxType:\"EnterpriseAlert\"},\"Unified CRLs require a Vault Enterprise license or HCP Plus cluster.\"),mdx(\"p\",null,`These are unauthenticated endpoints.`),mdx(\"div\",{className:\"alert alert-warning g-type-body\"},mdx(\"p\",null,mdx(\"strong\",{parentName:\"p\"},`Note`),`: As of Vault 1.11.0, these endpoints now serve a `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5280#section-5.1.2.1\"},`version 2`),` CRL response.`)),mdx(\"div\",{className:\"alert alert-warning g-type-body\"},mdx(\"p\",null,`Note: this endpoint accepts the `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`If-Modified-Since`),` header, to respond with\n304 Not Modified when the requested resource has not changed. This header\nneeds to be allowed on the PKI mount