o true to remove all invalid and\nexpired certificates from storage. A revoked storage entry is considered\ninvalid if the entry is empty, or the value within the entry is empty. If a\ncertificate is removed due to expiry, the entry will also be removed from the\nCRL, and the CRL will be rotated.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"tidy_revoked_cert_issuer_associations\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"#tidy_revoked_cert_issuer_associations\",\"aria-label\":\"tidy_revoked_cert_issuer_associations permalink\",\"className\":\"__permalink-lic\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`tidy_revoked_cert_issuer_associations`)),` `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`(bool: false)`),` - Set to true to associate\nrevoked certificates with their corresponding issuers; this improves the\nperformance of OCSP and CRL building, by shifting work to a tidy operation\ninstead.`))),mdx(\"div\",{className:\"alert alert-warning g-type-body\"},mdx(\"p\",null,`Note: With multiple issuers, a CA which issued a particular revoked\ncertificate may be removed and re-added, resulting in a different issuer\nID value. When building CRLs, these links are automatically updated for any\nmissing or added issuers, but during OCSP this value is computed and then\ndiscarded, potentially causing a performance penalty on each request.\nDuring regular CA operations, it is not necessary to run this operation.`)),mdx(\"br\",null),mdx(\"br\",null),\"It is suggested to run this tidy when removing or importing new issuers and on the first upgrade to a post-1.11 Vault version, but otherwise not to run it during automatic tidy operations.\",mdx(\"ul\",null,mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"tidy_expired_issuers\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"href\":\"#tidy_expired_issuers\",\"aria-label\